dashboard.definition:
{
  "title": "Cluster Colors",
  "description": "Per-clusterGroup color configuration added in v4.5.1. All panels use makeresults - no external data needed.",
  "dataSources": {
    "ds_map1": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "options": {
        "query": "| makeresults count=120\n| streamstats count as i\n| eval region=case(i<=30,\"northeast\",i<=60,\"westcoast\",i<=90,\"midwest\",1=1,\"southeast\")\n| eval latitude=case(region=\"northeast\",40.7+(i%7-3)*0.45,region=\"westcoast\",37.5+(i%7-3)*0.7,region=\"midwest\",41.8+(i%7-3)*0.45,1=1,32.0+(i%7-3)*0.7)\n| eval longitude=case(region=\"northeast\",-74.0+(i%5-2)*0.45,region=\"westcoast\",-121.0+(i%5-2)*0.7,region=\"midwest\",-87.6+(i%5-2)*0.45,1=1,-83.5+(i%5-2)*0.7)\n| eval clusterGroup=case(region=\"northeast\",\"servers\",region=\"westcoast\",\"routers\",region=\"midwest\",\"switches\",1=1,\"firewalls\")\n| table latitude, longitude, clusterGroup",
        "queryParameters": {
          "earliest": "-1m",
          "latest": "now"
        }
      },
      "name": "Cluster colors section 1"
    },
    "ds_map2": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "options": {
        "query": "| makeresults count=50\n| streamstats count as i\n| eval latitude=41.8+(i%7-3)*0.45\n| eval longitude=-87.6+(i%6-3)*0.45\n| eval clusterGroup=\"assets_prod\"\n| eval clusterBgColor=\"#9B59B6\"\n| eval clusterFgColor=\"#6C3483\"\n| table latitude, longitude, clusterGroup, clusterBgColor, clusterFgColor",
        "queryParameters": {
          "earliest": "-1m",
          "latest": "now"
        }
      },
      "name": "Cluster colors section 2"
    },
    "ds_map3": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "options": {
        "query": "| makeresults count=100\n| streamstats count as i\n| eval region=case(i<=25,\"northeast\",i<=50,\"westcoast\",i<=75,\"midwest\",1=1,\"southeast\")\n| eval latitude=case(region=\"northeast\",40.7+(i%7-3)*0.45,region=\"westcoast\",37.5+(i%6-3)*0.5,region=\"midwest\",41.8+(i%7-3)*0.45,1=1,32.0+(i%6-3)*0.5)\n| eval longitude=case(region=\"northeast\",-74.0+(i%5-2)*0.45,region=\"westcoast\",-122.0+(i%5-2)*0.5,region=\"midwest\",-87.6+(i%5-2)*0.45,1=1,-84.0+(i%5-2)*0.5)\n| eval clusterGroup=case(region=\"northeast\",\"dark_hosts\",region=\"westcoast\",\"staging\",region=\"midwest\",\"cdn\",1=1,\"unknown_group\")\n| table latitude, longitude, clusterGroup",
        "queryParameters": {
          "earliest": "-1m",
          "latest": "now"
        }
      },
      "name": "Cluster colors section 3"
    }
  },
  "visualizations": {
    "md_overview": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### Cluster Colors: clusterGroup color configuration\n\nAssign distinct colors to named marker cluster groups using the **Cluster Group Colors** option (`clusterGroupColors`), per-row SPL fields, or both together. Count labels automatically switch to white on dark backgrounds.\n\n**Note:** `clusterGroupColors` is a visualization **option** (in Dashboard Studio it is the `leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.clusterGroupColors` entry in the viz `options`). `clusterBgColor` and `clusterFgColor` are **SPL fields** returned as columns in your search results.\n\n| Name | Type | Description | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Cluster Group Colors | Option | Comma-separated `groupName:color` pairs. Supports hex, `rgba()` and named CSS colors. Use the reserved key `default` as a catch-all for group names not explicitly listed. | `servers:#E74C3C, routers:steelblue, default:#888` |\n| `clusterBgColor` | SPL field | Per-row override for the outer ring color of this row's `clusterGroup`. Takes priority over Cluster Group Colors. If only one SPL color field is present the other mirrors it. | `\\| eval clusterBgColor=\"#9B59B6\"` |\n| `clusterFgColor` | SPL field | Per-row override for the inner circle color of this row's `clusterGroup`. Takes priority over Cluster Group Colors. | `\\| eval clusterFgColor=\"#6C3483\"` |\n\n**Resolution order:** SPL fields, then Cluster Group Colors[groupName], then Cluster Group Colors[default], then the threshold fallback (green / yellow / orange).\n\n**Alpha:** hex and named colors automatically derive a 0.6-opacity outer ring and 0.8-opacity inner circle. `rgba()` values use your alpha as-is.\n"
      }
    },
    "viz_map1": {
      "type": "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_map1"
      },
      "options": {
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.cluster": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.clusterGroupColors": "servers:#E74C3C, routers:#3498DB, switches:#2ECC71, firewalls:#E67E22",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.autoFitAndZoom": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.autoFitAndZoomDelay": "500",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.defaultHeight": "500",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.mapCenterLat": "39.50",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.mapCenterLon": "-98.35",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.mapCenterZoom": "4",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.maxClusterRadius": "80",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.animate": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.showProgress": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.useOpenFreeMap": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.maplibreStylePreset": "positron"
      }
    },
    "viz_map2": {
      "type": "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_map2"
      },
      "options": {
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.cluster": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.clusterGroupColors": "assets_prod:#E74C3C",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.autoFitAndZoom": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.autoFitAndZoomDelay": "500",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.defaultHeight": "500",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.mapCenterLat": "41.8",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.mapCenterLon": "-87.6",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.mapCenterZoom": "11",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.maxClusterRadius": "80",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.animate": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.showProgress": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.useOpenFreeMap": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.maplibreStylePreset": "positron"
      }
    },
    "viz_map3": {
      "type": "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_map3"
      },
      "options": {
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.cluster": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.clusterGroupColors": "dark_hosts:#1A252F, staging:rgba(52,152,219,0.4), cdn:steelblue, default:#8E44AD",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.autoFitAndZoom": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.autoFitAndZoomDelay": "500",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.defaultHeight": "500",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.mapCenterLat": "39.50",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.mapCenterLon": "-98.35",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.mapCenterZoom": "4",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.maxClusterRadius": "80",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.animate": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.showProgress": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.useOpenFreeMap": "1",
        "leaflet_maps_app.maps-plus.maplibreStylePreset": "positron"
      }
    },
    "md_map1": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### 1. Formatter-driven colors\n\nFour cluster groups (`servers`, `routers`, `switches`, `firewalls`) spread across the US, each colored by the **Cluster Group Colors** option. The SPL only outputs `clusterGroup`; no color fields are needed. Zoom in to see individual markers: clusters dissolve and re-form as you zoom.\n\nThe option on this map: `servers:#E74C3C, routers:#3498DB, switches:#2ECC71, firewalls:#E67E22`\n\n### The SPL\n\n```spl\n| makeresults count=120\n| streamstats count as i\n| eval region=case(i<=30,\"northeast\",i<=60,\"westcoast\",i<=90,\"midwest\",1=1,\"southeast\")\n... (latitude and longitude: spread around each region's city center, using i%7 and i%5)\n| eval clusterGroup=case(region=\"northeast\",\"servers\",region=\"westcoast\",\"routers\",region=\"midwest\",\"switches\",1=1,\"firewalls\")\n| table latitude, longitude, clusterGroup\n```\n\n### How it works\n\n1. `makeresults count=120` creates 120 empty rows and `streamstats count as i` numbers them.\n2. `eval region=case(i<=30,...)` splits the rows into four regions of about 30 rows each.\n3. `latitude` and `longitude` place each row around its region's city, using `i%7` and `i%5` to spread the points.\n4. `clusterGroup` is set from the region (`servers`, `routers`, `switches`, `firewalls`). Rows in different groups never cluster together.\n5. `table latitude, longitude, clusterGroup` leaves out all color fields, so the colors come from the `clusterGroupColors` option.\n\n### Field formats and rules\n\n| Field / option | Format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `latitude`, `longitude` | decimal degrees | Exact lowercase names; required. |\n| `clusterGroup` | any string, default `default` | Different values never cluster together. Avoid `one`, `two` and `three`: they clash with Maps+ CSS classes. |\n| `clusterGroupColors` (option) | `group:color,group:color` | Hex, `rgba()` or named CSS colors; key `default` is the catch-all. |\n\n### Try it\n\n- In the viz options, change `servers:#E74C3C` to `servers:crimson` and reload.\n- Add a fifth `clusterGroup` value in the `case()` and give it a color in the option.\n"
      }
    },
    "md_map2": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### 2. SPL field override\n\nAdd `clusterBgColor` and `clusterFgColor` to the results to override the option color at query time. This is useful when color is data-driven, for example by environment, severity or ownership.\n\nHere the option declares `assets_prod:#E74C3C` (red), but the query adds purple override fields. The clusters render purple: SPL always wins. If only one of the two fields is present the other mirrors it, so `clusterBgColor` alone gives a flat color.\n\n### The SPL\n\n```spl\n| makeresults count=50\n| streamstats count as i\n| eval latitude=41.8+(i%7-3)*0.45\n| eval longitude=-87.6+(i%6-3)*0.45\n| eval clusterGroup=\"assets_prod\"\n| eval clusterBgColor=\"#9B59B6\"\n| eval clusterFgColor=\"#6C3483\"\n| table latitude, longitude, clusterGroup, clusterBgColor, clusterFgColor\n```\n\n### How it works\n\n1. `makeresults count=50` and `streamstats count as i` create 50 numbered rows.\n2. `latitude` and `longitude` scatter them around Chicago using `i%7` and `i%6`.\n3. `clusterGroup=\"assets_prod\"` puts every row in one group.\n4. `clusterBgColor` sets the outer ring and `clusterFgColor` the inner circle.\n5. Both fields are in `table`, so they are read for every row and beat the `assets_prod` color in the option.\n\n### Field formats and rules\n\n| Field / option | Format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `latitude`, `longitude` | decimal degrees | Exact lowercase names; required. |\n| `clusterGroup` | any string | Different values never cluster together. |\n| `clusterBgColor` | any CSS color | Outer ring; per-row override that takes priority over `clusterGroupColors`. |\n| `clusterFgColor` | any CSS color | Inner circle; per-row override. The other field mirrors it when only one is present. |\n| `clusterGroupColors` (option) | `group:color` | Still set here (`assets_prod:#E74C3C`) but overridden by the row fields. |\n\n### Try it\n\n- Delete `clusterFgColor` from `table` and see the flat purple ring-and-circle.\n- Remove both color fields from `table`: the clusters fall back to red from the option.\n"
      }
    },
    "md_map3": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### 3. Color formats, default fallback and contrast labels\n\nFour groups, each with a different color format, plus a group with no explicit color. The option on this map:\n\n`dark_hosts:#1A252F, staging:rgba(52,152,219,0.4), cdn:steelblue, default:#8E44AD`\n\n`dark_hosts` uses a near-black color, so the count label switches to **white**. The `unknown_group` markers in the Southeast have no mapping and fall through to the `default` purple.\n\n### The SPL\n\n```spl\n| makeresults count=100\n| streamstats count as i\n| eval region=case(i<=25,\"northeast\",i<=50,\"westcoast\",i<=75,\"midwest\",1=1,\"southeast\")\n... (latitude and longitude: spread around each region's city center)\n| eval clusterGroup=case(region=\"northeast\",\"dark_hosts\",region=\"westcoast\",\"staging\",region=\"midwest\",\"cdn\",1=1,\"unknown_group\")\n| table latitude, longitude, clusterGroup\n```\n\n### How it works\n\n1. `makeresults count=100` and `streamstats count as i` create 100 numbered rows.\n2. `region=case(i<=25,...)` splits them into four regions of 25 rows.\n3. `latitude` and `longitude` place each row around its region's city.\n4. `clusterGroup` is `dark_hosts`, `staging`, `cdn` or `unknown_group`, by region.\n5. The option has no entry for `unknown_group`, so Maps+ uses `default:#8E44AD`.\n\n### Field formats and rules\n\n| Color format | Example | Alpha behavior |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hex | `#E74C3C` | Derived automatically: 0.6 outer ring, 0.8 inner circle |\n| RGBA | `rgba(52,152,219,0.4)` | Used as-is |\n| Named CSS | `steelblue`, `crimson` | Derived automatically: 0.6 / 0.8 |\n\n| Field / option | Format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `latitude`, `longitude` | decimal degrees | Required, lowercase. |\n| `clusterGroup` | any string | Unlisted names use the `default` key of the option. |\n\n### Try it\n\n- Change `default:#8E44AD` to `default:orange` to recolor the Southeast.\n- Rename one `clusterGroup` value in the query so it no longer matches the option and watch it take the default color.\n"
      }
    }
  },
  "layout": {
